  "description": "ZUYZAW crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C212 H168 Dy14 N48 O66 P10,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.720-4.073 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.66-118.02°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy14(EDDC)4(opch)4(O3PC10H7)10(OAc)6(H2O)4]·xH2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
